# Probe 35 (scripts/probe_even_chart_options.py): the labels and legend options the archived charts were never probed for, before promoting them into the core.
# Seen (bridge captures, then a real refresh + Ctrl+S): all seven candidates drew as predicted (P1-P7). Area chart with objects.labels.show = true showed data labels on both series (600/600 on Target Amount, 200/300 on Total Amount) — the one I was least sure of, since probe 23 only ever put that object on the column and the three stacked charts. objects.legend.position 'Right' moved the area chart's legend and the stacked column's legend to the right; objects.legend.show = false hid the legend on the area chart, the stacked column, the 100% stacked column and the stacked bar. The control on page 2 (an area chart with no options) kept its legend at the bottom, so the three area variants are genuinely changed and not just legend-less. The save rewrote only the two visuals on page 2 (the active page): both kept their objects exactly as written — the stacked bar still legend show false, the control still no objects — and gained only Desktop's usual $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 and its condition-less auto filterConfig, plus pages.json activePageName. The six visuals on page 1 were not rewritten at all, so what Blueprint and the probe wrote is still on disk byte for byte. All content invented.

